---
const title = 'Agent CRM — Relationship memory for your agent';
const description = 'An experimental, local-first relationship database for shell-capable AI agents. Structured records, useful context, and one SQLite database you control.';
const canonical = Astro.site ? new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site) : undefined;
const social = Astro.site ? new URL('/social.svg', Astro.site) : '/social.svg';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    {canonical && <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:image" content={social} />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="Agent CRM: relationship memory, locally held. Your agent → Agent CRM → SQLite." />
    {canonical && <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />}
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="wrap masthead">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Agent CRM home"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">a<span>:</span></span> Agent CRM</a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a href="/docs/">Docs</a><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/agent-crm">npm <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/francanete/agent-crm">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="wrap hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status" aria-hidden="true"></span> Local-first / open source / experimental</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Good relationships.<br /><em>Durable memory.</em></h1>
          <p class="lede">Give your agent a place to remember people, conversations, and what comes next.</p>
          <p class="intro">Agent CRM is a schema-aware relationship database for shell-capable AI agents. A deterministic CLI. One local SQLite database. No CRM server or account.</p>
          <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/agent-crm">View package on npm <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
          <p class="release">Published on npm · Node.js 24 · MIT licensed<br />Current package: 0.1.0. Pages covering newer main-only behavior are labelled.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="terminal">
          <figcaption><span class="terminal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> A SMALL, LOCAL BEGINNING <span>bash</span></figcaption>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <p class="comment"># Install the published package</p>
            <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Bash example installing Agent CRM and using a temporary database"><code>npm install --global agent-crm
export AGENTCRM_DB="$(mktemp -d)/crm.db"
agentcrm init --json

<span class="comment"># Look before you remember</span>
agentcrm search "ana@example.com" \
  --object person --json

<span class="comment"># A structured record, not a loose note</span>
agentcrm record create person \
  --values {'\'{"name":"Ana",\n    "email":"ana@example.com"}\''} --json</code></pre>
            <div class="terminal-note"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span> Fake contact. Real CLI commands.<br />No simulated output.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-footer">YOUR MACHINE <span>SQLite · no runtime network requests</span></div>
        </figure>
      </section>
      <section class="principles" aria-label="Core design">
        <div class="wrap principle-grid"><p><strong>Local by default.</strong><span>Your files, your database.</span></p><p><strong>Built for agent tools.</strong><span>Explicit commands, structured JSON.</span></p><p><strong>Memory with context.</strong><span>People connected to what matters.</span></p></div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap capabilities" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Beyond a contact list</p><h2 id="capabilities-title">Less re-explaining.<br />More picking up where you left off.</h2><p>Keep the details that make a relationship useful—not just a name in a text file.</p></div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article><span class="index">[01]</span><h3>Remember the shape<br />of a relationship.</h3><p>People, organizations, interactions, and follow-ups share one store. Directed relationships connect them; typed custom objects let your model grow.</p><a href="/docs/cli-reference/#schema-commands">Explore the schema <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
          <article><span class="index">[02]</span><h3>Bring context to<br />the next conversation.</h3><p>Search with SQLite FTS5 and retrieve bounded relationship context before a meeting. No embeddings or external retrieval service required.</p><a href="/docs/workflows/">See the workflow <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
          <article><span class="index">[03]</span><h3>Make changes<br />you can account for.</h3><p>Schema validation, transactions, exact-retry idempotency, and immutable mutation history give agents explicit rules for writing durable data.</p><a href="/docs/cli-reference/#idempotent-mutations">Understand retries <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap system" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="system-title">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">02 / A small, deliberate system</p><h2 id="system-title">Your agent talks.<br />The CLI keeps the record.</h2><p>Keep your existing shell-capable agent. The bundled Skill teaches it to inspect schema, search before creating, and return useful answers instead of raw tool output.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/agent-setup/">Connect an agent and database <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
        <ol class="flow"><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Your agent</strong><small>Shell access + portable Agent Skill</small></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>agentcrm</strong><small>Validated commands + JSON contracts</small></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Your SQLite database</strong><small>Records + relationships + history</small></div></li></ol>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap boundary" aria-labelledby="boundary-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Know the boundary</p><div><h2 id="boundary-title">Local storage.<br />Not a blanket privacy promise.</h2><p>Agent CRM makes no runtime network requests. But your agent host, model provider, and messaging channel may receive the data it reads. The database and exports are not encrypted by Agent CRM.</p><p>This is experimental software—not a hosted dashboard, cloud sync service, or production-readiness claim. Back up before upgrades. Archive preserves history; it is not erasure.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs/privacy-security/">Read the privacy model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
      <section class="wrap closing"><div><p class="eyebrow">Start small. Use fake data first.</p><h2>A useful memory starts<br />with one local record.</h2></div><a class="button" href="/docs/getting-started/">Install & try Agent CRM <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap"><a class="brand" href="/">Agent CRM</a><p>Local relationship memory. Open source, MIT.</p><nav aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href="/docs/">Documentation</a><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/agent-crm">npm</a><a href="https://github.com/francanete/agent-crm/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribute</a><a href="https://github.com/francanete/agent-crm/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Security</a></nav></footer>
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  /* Restrained, grid-led public site; original scoped layout below. */
  html body { background:#fff; color:#171717; font-family:Inter,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased; }
  body .wrap { width:min(1200px,calc(100% - 4rem)); }
  body .masthead { min-height:80px; border-color:#e8e8e8; }
  body .brand { font-weight:650; font-size:1.1rem; }
  body .mark { background:#171717; color:#fff; border-radius:6px; font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Consolas,monospace; width:30px; height:30px; font-size:21px; }
  body .masthead nav, body footer nav { color:#525252; }
  body .hero { display:block; padding:6rem 3rem 0; border-inline:1px solid #ededed; }
  body .hero-copy { text-align:center; }
  body .hero .eyebrow { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; border:1px solid #e5e5e5; border-radius:99px; padding:.45rem .85rem; background:#fafafa; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.05em; }
  body .eyebrow { color:#626262; font-weight:500; }
  body .status { background:#237b53; width:6px; height:6px; }
  body h1 { font:650 clamp(3.2rem,6.5vw,5.6rem)/1.04 Inter,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; letter-spacing:-.065em; margin:1.8rem 0 1.5rem; }
  body h1 em { font:inherit; font-style:normal; color:#737373; letter-spacing:inherit; }
  body h1 .desktop { display:none; }
  body .lede { color:#525252; font-size:1.2rem; max-width:36rem; margin:0 auto 1rem; }
  body .intro { color:#626262; font-size:.9rem; max-width:39rem; margin:0 auto; }
  body .actions { justify-content:center; gap:.8rem; margin-top:2rem; }
  body .button, body .actions .text-link { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-height:46px; border:1px solid #171717; border-radius:6px; padding:.65rem 1.35rem; gap:1.6rem; background:#171717; color:#fff; font-size:.85rem; font-weight:550; text-decoration:none; transition:background .15s,border-color .15s; }
  body .button:hover { background:#333; border-color:#333; }
  body .actions .text-link { background:#fff; border-color:#dedede; color:#171717; }
  body .actions .text-link:hover { background:#f5f5f5; border-color:#aaa; }
  body .release { color:#737373; font-size:.7rem; line-height:1.9; margin:1.2rem 0 0; }
  body .terminal { transform:none; max-width:740px; margin:4rem auto 0; border:1px solid #333; border-radius:9px 9px 0 0; background:#0a0a0a; color:#ededed; box-shadow:0 24px 60px -25px #00000050; overflow:hidden; }
  body .terminal figcaption { background:#141414; border-color:#292929; color:#b5b5b5; padding:.9rem 1.5rem; font-size:.65rem; letter-spacing:.06em; }
  body .terminal-dot { background:#737373; box-shadow:12px 0 #525252,24px 0 #404040; margin-right:1.9rem; width:7px; height:7px; }
  body .terminal-body { padding:1.5rem 2rem; }
  body .terminal pre { font-size:.8rem; line-height:1.85; color:#ededed; }
  body .terminal .comment { color:#a1a1a1; }
  body .terminal figcaption > span:last-child { color:#a1a1a1; }
  body .terminal-note { border-color:#292929; color:#a1a1a1; font-size:.7rem; }
  body .terminal-footer { background:#141414; border-color:#292929; color:#a1a1a1; padding:.75rem 1.5rem; font-size:.6rem; }
  body .principles { border-color:#e8e8e8; background:#fff; }
  body .principle-grid { gap:0; border-left:1px solid #e8e8e8; }
  body .principle-grid p { margin:0; padding:2rem; border-right:1px solid #e8e8e8; font-size:.8rem; }
  body .principle-grid strong { color:#171717; font-weight:600; }
  body .principle-grid p span { color:#626262; }
  body .capabilities { padding:6rem 0 0; }
  body .section-heading { text-align:center; max-width:none; padding-inline:1rem; }
  body h2 { font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.1vw,2.7rem); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.05em; line-height:1.18; color:#171717; }
  body .section-heading > p:last-child { color:#626262; font-size:.95rem; max-width:none; }
  body .feature-grid { gap:0; margin-top:3rem; border:1px solid #e8e8e8; }
  body .feature-grid article { display:flex; flex-direction:column; padding:2.3rem 2rem; border-top:0; min-width:0; }
  body .feature-grid article + article { border-left:1px solid #e8e8e8; }
  body .index { color:#737373; font-size:.65rem; margin-bottom:2.5rem; }
  body .feature-grid h3 { color:#171717; font-size:1.3rem; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.035em; line-height:1.35; }
  body .feature-grid p { color:#626262; font-size:.86rem; line-height:1.8; margin-bottom:1.8rem; }
  body .feature-grid a { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-top:auto; color:#171717; font-size:.8rem; }
  body .system { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:5rem; padding:5rem 2rem; background:#fff; border:1px solid #e8e8e8; border-top:0; }
  body .system h2 { font-size:clamp(1.8rem,2.7vw,2.4rem); }
  body .system p:not(.eyebrow), body .boundary p:not(.eyebrow) { color:#626262; font-size:.9rem; }
  body .text-link { color:#171717; }
  body .flow { margin:auto 0; padding:0; }
  body .flow li { position:relative; padding:1.3rem; border:1px solid #e5e5e5; border-radius:6px; background:#fafafa; gap:1rem; }
  body .flow li + li { margin-top:1.6rem; }
  body .flow li:last-child { border:1px solid #e5e5e5; }
  body .flow li + li::before { content:''; position:absolute; height:1.6rem; width:1px; background:#d4d4d4; left:2rem; bottom:100%; }
  body .flow li > span { background:transparent; color:#737373; border:0; font-size:.65rem; }
  body .flow strong { color:#171717; font-size:.9rem; font-weight:550; }
  body .flow small { color:#626262; font-size:.72rem; }
  body .boundary { grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr; padding:5rem 2rem; gap:4rem; border:1px solid #e8e8e8; border-top:0; }
  body .closing { padding:4rem 2rem; border:1px solid #e8e8e8; border-top:0; background:#fafafa; }
  body .closing h2 { font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem); }
  body footer { padding-block:2.5rem; border:0; }
  body footer p { color:#737373; font-size:.7rem; }
  body .skip { background:#171717; color:#fff; }
  body a:focus-visible, body pre:focus-visible { outline:2px solid #0068d6; outline-offset:5px; }
  body ::selection { background:#dbeafe; color:#171717; }
  @media(max-width:1000px) {
    body .hero { padding-inline:2rem; }
    body .system { gap:2rem; }
    body .feature-grid article { padding:2rem 1.5rem; }
    body .terminal-footer { flex-direction:row; }
  }
  @media(max-width:760px) {
    body .wrap { width:calc(100% - 2rem); }
    body .masthead { min-height:72px; }
    body .hero { padding:3.5rem 1rem 0; }
    body h1 { font-size:clamp(2.45rem,8.4vw,4rem); }
    body .hero .eyebrow { font-size:.5rem; letter-spacing:.015em; padding:.4rem .6rem; }
    body .lede { font-size:1rem; }
    body .intro { font-size:.8rem; }
    body .actions { gap:.6rem; }
    body .button, body .actions .text-link { font-size:.78rem; padding-inline:1rem; gap:.9rem; }
    body .terminal { margin:2.5rem -.5rem 0; }
    body .terminal figcaption { padding:.8rem; font-size:.5rem; }
    body .terminal-body { padding:1.1rem .85rem; }
    body .terminal pre { font-size:.64rem; }
    body .terminal-note { font-size:.6rem; }
    body .terminal-footer { flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.3rem; padding:.65rem .85rem; font-size:.5rem; }
    body .principle-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:0; }
    body .principle-grid p { padding:1.2rem 1.5rem; font-size:.8rem; }
    body .principle-grid p + p { border-top:1px solid #e8e8e8; }
    body .capabilities { padding-top:3.5rem; }
    body .section-heading > p:last-child { font-size:.85rem; }
    body .feature-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:0; margin-top:2rem; }
    body .feature-grid article { padding:1.5rem; }
    body .feature-grid article + article { border-left:0; border-top:1px solid #e8e8e8; }
    body .index { margin-bottom:1rem; }
    body .system { grid-template-columns:1fr; padding:2.5rem 1.5rem; gap:2rem; }
    body .flow li { padding:1rem; }
    body .boundary { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:0; padding:2.5rem 1.5rem; }
    body .closing { padding:2.5rem 1.5rem; }
    body footer { padding-block:2rem; }
  }
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce) { body .button, body .actions .text-link { transition:none; } }
</style>
